{
  "id": "COMPOUND:223 - PROTEIN:1379",
  "verbalization": "Aminosalicylic acid appears to have a shared target relationship with G-protein coupled estrogen receptor 1 through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Aminosalicylic acid acts as a target of several molecules, including 72 kDa type IV collagenase and Diacylglycerol kinase gamma, which in turn target the G-protein coupled estrogen receptor 1. This indicates a potential network of interactions where Aminosalicylic acid may influence the receptor through different molecular intermediates. The presence of multiple distinct targets pointing to the same receptor suggests that Aminosalicylic acid may exert its effects via diverse mechanisms, possibly through different pathways or by modulating the activity of these intermediates. The integration of these pathways highlights the receptor's role as a central node in a complex regulatory network, possibly involved in cellular signaling processes.",
